# Shared AI credential management — manual API tests (REST Client / JetBrains HTTP).
#
# 1. Copy this file to ai.rest (gitignored — keeps your real key out of git).
# 2. Generate an encryption key and set it before starting the API:
#      AI_ENCRYPTION_KEY=$(openssl rand -base64 32)
#    (in .env, or the process environment). Then: go run ./cmd/api
# 3. Create a tenant + tenant key via the admin console / TUI, fill in @tenantKey.
# 4. Paste your real Anthropic key into the POST body and Send Request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:18080
@tenant = pem
# A TUI-issued tenant API key (key_...) or an HS256 JWT with a matching tenant claim.
@tenantKey = key_yourKeyId.yourSecret

### Store a bring-your-own Anthropic key — validated, then stored encrypted.
# Response is masked metadata only (never echoes the key).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/ai/credentials
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantKey}}
X-KD-Tenant: {{tenant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "api_key": "sk-ant-REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_KEY",
  "model": "claude-sonnet-5"
}

### List stored credentials (masked)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/ai/credentials
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantKey}}
X-KD-Tenant: {{tenant}}

### Delete the Anthropic credential
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/ai/credentials/anthropic
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantKey}}
X-KD-Tenant: {{tenant}}

### Reject a bad key — expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/ai/credentials
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantKey}}
X-KD-Tenant: {{tenant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "api_key": "not-a-real-key" }
